---
title: Baked Feta Pasta
servings: 6
cuisine: mediterranean
main_protein: dairy
prep_time: "5 minutes"
cook_time: "35 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
  - feta
  - pasta
  - tomatoes
source: https://feelgoodfoodie.net/recipe/baked-feta-pasta/
image: ../obsidian/attachments/baked-feta-pasta.jpg
leftover_portions: 2
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 400°F
  - Mince 2 garlic cloves
  - Chop 0.25 cup basil, plus more for serving
  - Bring a pot of salted water to a boil
---
Preheat #oven{} to 400°F. Place @cherry tomatoes{2%pints} in an #oven-safe baking dish{}. Pour @extra virgin olive oil{0.5%cup} on top and season with @salt{0.25%tsp} and @black pepper{0.25%tsp}. Toss until combined.

Place the @feta cheese{8%oz} block in the middle of the baking dish surrounded by tomatoes, flipping a couple times to coat with oil and seasoning.

Bake for ~{35%minutes} until tomatoes burst and feta melts.

Cook @cavatappi pasta{8%oz} in salted water according to package directions until al dente. Drain, reserving ½ cup cooking liquid.

Immediately add @garlic{2%cloves}, minced, and @fresh basil{0.25%cup}, packed and chopped, to the tomato and feta mixture and toss to combine.

Transfer cooked pasta to the baking dish and toss together. Garnish with fresh basil and serve warm.
